    "title": "For inclusive festivals",
    "subtitle": null,
    "author": "Kuhu Adhikary,Rema Sundar",
    "published_at": null,
    "image_url": null,
    "image_caption": null,
    "content_html": "<div class=\"articlebodycontent col-xl-9 col-lg-12 col-md-12 col-sm-12 col-12\" id=\"content-body-71694219\"><div class=\"schemaDiv\" id=\"schemaDiv\"><p>India’s long festival season is marked by the gift of giving. The various festivals have as an underlying objective compassion and care for fellow beings.</p><p>But what is “care” all about? The simple-sounding four-letter word carries depth and meaning. “Take care” is a commonly used phrase in daily interactions. Care is most commonly paired with health, bringing a broad lens of care to that perspective. “Childcare” has been in vogue for some time, while “senior care” or “elder care” is a relatively new concept.</p></div><div class=\"articleblock-container\" id=\"arthardpv\"></div><div class=\"update-publish-time article-published-time-end\"><p class=\"publish-time-new\"> Published <span>- November 15, 2026 05:38 am IST</span></p></div><div class=\"comments-shares share-page flex print-hide\" data-artid=\"71694219\" data-title=\"For inclusive festivals\" data-url=\"https://www.thehindu.com/opinion/open-page/for-inclusive-festivals/article71694219.ece\"><div class=\"left\"><div class=\"share\"><button class=\"btn share-btn\" data-ga-labelclick=\"ArticleShare\"></button><ul class=\"share-list bottom\" style=\"display: none;\"><li class=\"copy-link\" data-cf-modified-3c6848d276cb8041c76594be-=\"\" onclick=\"if (!window.__cfRLUnblockHandlers) return false; copytext('https://www.thehindu.com/opinion/open-page/for-inclusive-festivals/article71694219.ece');\">\n                Copy link  \n                        \n            </li><li class=\"email\"><a href=\"mailto:?subject=For%20inclusive%20festivals&amp;amp;body=Check%20out%20this%20link%20https%3A%2F%2Fwww.thehindu.com%2Fopinion%2Fopen-page%2Ffor-inclusive-festivals%2Farticle71694219.ece\" target=\"_self\">\n                    Email     \n                                \n                </a></li><li class=\"facebook\" data-cf-modified-3c6848d